---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
        title="Status — CivicBrands"
        description="Operational posture and known status for CivicBrands public surfaces."
>
    <section class="section">
        <p class="eyebrow">Status</p>

        <div class="measure">
            <h1>Operational posture.</h1>
            <p>
                Status means two things here: whether the public surfaces are expected to be reachable,
                and whether the information inside them should be treated as current, reviewed, or
                best-effort. Both matter.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="status-list">
            <section>
                <h2>CivicBrands main site</h2>
                <dl class="entry-meta">
                    <dt>Surface</dt>
                    <dd><a href="https://civicbrands.org">civicbrands.org</a></dd>
                    <dt>Posture</dt>
                    <dd>Static-first publication and records surface.</dd>
                    <dt>Expected Availability</dt>
                    <dd>High, subject to hosting and DNS availability.</dd>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>KC directory</h2>
                <dl class="entry-meta">
                    <dt>Surface</dt>
                    <dd><a href="/kc">civicbrands.org/kc</a></dd>
                    <dt>Posture</dt>
                    <dd>Human-reviewed, best-effort resource directory with correction pathways and practical access guidance.</dd>
                    <dt>Urgent Corrections</dt>
                    <dd><a href="/kc/suggest">Suggest / correct</a> or email <a href="mailto:corrections@mail.civicbrands.org">corrections@mail.civicbrands.org</a>.</dd>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Forecast</h2>
                <dl class="entry-meta">
                    <dt>Surface</dt>
                    <dd><a href="https://forecast.civicbrands.org">forecast.civicbrands.org</a></dd>
                    <dt>Posture</dt>
                    <dd>Operational public information infrastructure. Data and interfaces may evolve as sources are added.</dd>
                    <dt>Reference</dt>
                    <dd><a href="/work/forecast">Forecast work entry</a></dd>
                </dl>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="measure">
            <p>
                If a public page is down, a critical phone number fails, or a listed service is turning
                people away, treat that as actionable. Send the correction through the most direct path
                available. We would rather fix the record than preserve the appearance of certainty.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
